            <ArticleTitle>Health-related quality of life among participants in the SMART weight loss trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>276-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.apnr.2011.08.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0897-1897(11)00059-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity has been associated with a decreased health-related quality of life (HRQoL); however, the association between weight change and HRQoL is unclear. This secondary analysis of the SMART (Self Monitoring And Recording using Technology) trial, a clinical trial of behavioral weight loss treatment, provides evidence that quality of life improves with weight loss.</AbstractText>
